<title>JAPAN: Tokyo rubber market closed for holiday.</title>
<headline>Tokyo rubber market closed for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese rubber markets were closed on Monday for a holiday. The markets reopen on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Kobe rubber futures were lower across the board in the after-hours session on Friday, pressured by selling from trade houses, traders said.</p>
<p>Prices ranged from 0.1 yen to 1.4 yen per kg lower than the day's close. Benchmark February was 0.5 yen weaker at 140.0 yen. Volume was 5,364 lots.</p>
</text>
